The Kerala Money-Lenders Act, 1958
to be recovered specifically by way of interest or otherwise, but does not include any sum charged by a lender in
accordance with the provisions of this Act or any other law for the time being in force, for or on account of costs, charges
or expenses;
(4)
"licence" means a money-lender's licence granted under this Act;
(4A)
"licensing authority" means an officer or authority appointed by the Government to perform the functions of a licensing
authority under this Act;
